error[M0275]: unexpected token 'else', expected a block `{ ... }`: `switch` and `do` always take a block, and so do the branches or body of `if`/`while`/`for` when the condition or head is an unparenthesized compound expression (a call, index, projection, or operator application); parenthesize it to keep bare branches — an unspaced `(`/`[` after a bare identifier continues the condition (`if c[i] ...` indexes `c`), a spaced one starts the branch (`if c [i] ...`)
    ┌─ syntax-head-tight-index.mo:4:25
  4 │  let a : [Nat] = if c[1] else [];
    │                          ^^^^ 
